{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic final class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int totalVertices = scanner.nextInt();\n        double targetProbability = scanner.nextDouble();\n        int left = 0;\n        int right = totalVertices - 1;\n        while (true) {\n            int mid = (left + right) / 2;\n            if (left == right) {\n                System.out.println(left);\n                return;\n            }\n            double prob = computeProbability(mid, totalVertices);\n            if (prob >= targetProbability) {\n                right = mid;\n            } else {\n                left = mid + 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static double computeProbability(int m, int n) {\n        long totalWays = combination(n, 3);\n        double numerator = 0.0;\n        numerator += combination(m, 3);\n        numerator += (double) combination(m, 2) * combination(n - m, 1);\n        numerator += 0.5 * combination(m, 1) * combination(n - m, 2);\n        return numerator / totalWays;\n    }\n\n    private static long combination(int n, int k) {\n        if (k > n) return 0;\n        if (k == n) return 1;\n        long result = 1L;\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            result *= (n - i);\n        }\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            result /= i;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long combination(int n, int k) {\n    if (k > n) return 0;\n    if (k == n) return 1;\n    long long result = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        result *= (n - i);\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n        result /= i;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\ndouble computeProbability(int m, int n) {\n    long long totalWays = combination(n, 3);\n    double numerator = 0.0;\n    numerator += combination(m, 3);\n    numerator += (double) combination(m, 2) * combination(n - m, 1);\n    numerator += 0.5 * combination(m, 1) * combination(n - m, 2);\n    return numerator / totalWays;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int totalVertices;\n    double targetProbability;\n    cin >> totalVertices >> targetProbability;\n    int left = 0;\n    int right = totalVertices - 1;\n    while (true) {\n        int mid = (left + right) / 2;\n        if (left == right) {\n            cout << left << endl;\n            return 0;\n        }\n        double prob = computeProbability(mid, totalVertices);\n        if (prob >= targetProbability) {\n            right = mid;\n        } else {\n            left = mid + 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0012224590172991157, -2.2053474822314456e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0007154765771701932, -2.407998726994265e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.4741021990776062, -0.5761223435401917, -8.904537389753386e-05, 0.0, -6.556